---
/* /calendar/: three ways in. A device that has already said who it is (the shared role
   preference) goes straight to that page; everyone else picks a door. Each door is a plain link
   to a page that is drawn at build time, so this works with JavaScript off. */
import CalendarShell from '../../components/CalendarShell.astro';
---
<CalendarShell title="Calendar" role="door" description="What is next, how long it takes and what it needs: an activity with a child, a course for yourself, or a class plan by date. No account, and anything you don’t get to simply waits.">
  <div class="cal-page">
    <header class="cal-top">
      <h1>Calendar</h1>
      <p class="cal-lede">What is next, how long it takes and what it needs. Who is it for?</p>
    </header>
    <ul class="cal-doors">
      <li><a class="cal-door" href="/calendar/parent/" data-role="parent"><strong>With a child</strong><span>One hands-on activity for ages 5 to 10 on the days that suit you, and one list of what to gather.</span></a></li>
      <li><a class="cal-door" href="/calendar/student/" data-role="student"><strong>For myself</strong><span>Keep up with a course one lesson at a time, or take the biology for the MCAT in order. No dates unless you ask for them.</span></a></li>
      <li><a class="cal-door" href="/calendar/teacher/" data-role="teacher"><strong>For my class</strong><span>A class plan by date, with the standard each lesson serves. For now it is a sample to try.</span></a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="cal-foot">Free, with no account and no email address. The plan stays on this device.</p>
  </div>
</CalendarShell>
